do you think that margaret ferrer should  resign as an mp  i think she should resign as an mp i  think she has lost the trust of our  constituents and i think  in terms of the way that we have to deal  with this global pandemic we need to  send out the message that people must  comply with the rules and for anybody to  break the rules  it's putting people at risk for a member  of parliament to break rules in such a  negligent and haphazard way putting the  lives in the health of  workers at risk and for people who work  on trains and in parliament  is really unforgivable and we need to  send a very strong message that this  will not be tolerated  so if if you get your way and she does  resign they'll of course be a  by-election  what would labour's position be on a  second independence referendum  in that by-election well our position is  absolutely clear the scottish executive  committee which is the ruling  committee of the scottish labor party  passed and reaffirmed  its position back in may and that  position is to  go into the election next year against  independence as we always have been  and against the second independent  referendum and come out of that election  with exactly the same position  but if the snp win uh the  majority next year's scottish parliament  elections would they have a mandate for  another referendum  well i think these hypothetical  questions are something that we should  be putting on the background or during  this global pandemic your first  questions on  whether or not an smp mp would be  spreading the virus across the united  kingdom by  traveling to and from parliament and  that's what the scottish people want us  to concentrate at the moment they want  us to go into that election you know we  have a post-covered recovery plan they  want us to come out with that election  trying to  sort the economy sort of people's jobs  and protect their livelihoods and to  consistently have these  hypothetical questions so kirsten has  gone into  the leadership of the labour party with  its new leadership and said quite  clearly that he wants to be leader of  the whole of the united kingdom  in 2024 he wants to make sure that  scotland isn't independent and he  doesn't want a second independence  referendum so those are pretty clear  positions i think all these  hypotheticals we need to move on is not  the priorities of the scottish people  and if i could just very quickly say  that in the recent poll and release the  last two polls actually  a second independence referendum just  made it into the top 10 when you add  those who desperately wanted one to  those who desperately didn't want one so  it's not the priorities of the scottish  people  and we have to concentrate on those and  that's what we're doing in the election  that's what we'll continue to do after  the election  you know you can kind of criticize us  for not asking enough about coronavirus  for asking about scottish independence  for  asking hypothetical questions but i feel  like the problem is that  if journalists feel that they're not  quite clear what labour's position is  in response to this question then  they're just going to keep asking  the question again kier starman back in  january so the snp  will have a mandate for another  referendum if they win next year he  added this is a question for scotland  and the people of scotland  if there's a majority it has to be  looked at in westminster  it feels as if you're not being straight  what would the position be  well this isn't a fight for the labour  party to have we won't be  empowered at westminster come may 2021  unless there is some  kind of general election before then i  doubt that will it happen  with you at all on something that is  such an important issue  and therefore kirsten has been pretty  clear he wants to take forward  a constitutional convention that looks  at a federal estate across the united  kingdom he wants to  look at how the house of lords operates  he wants a new constitutional settlement  going into the  2024 general election that's what will  be in the labour party manifesto the  labour party  couldn't be clearer in fact the reason  that we're in some of the  difficulties in terms of electoral  difficulties in scotland is because we  are clear on this principal position  we're against independence  and against the second independent  referendum and i really do think that  this is uh  couldn't be clearer and if you look at  douglas ross and in terms of the new  scottish  conservative leader he said quickly  though that many in his own party  don't believe in the union and really  the biggest threat to the united kingdom  at the moment  even more than any nationalist in fact  is the conservative unionist party with  the way they're dealing with brexit  the way they're dealing with covet and  the way that the scottish people see  this current prime minister  um of kobe cases of course uh top of the  political gender uh for everyone  at the minute we saw of course those  record number of cases posted yesterday  because of a technical error  how concerned are you about the current  situation  well i think the common situation with  corbett i think the government have  messed it up they've wasted the summer  it's quite clear that tests and trace  isn't working properly the testing  system  is collapsing and indeed it may have  been a technical error but it's just  another error layered on top of all the  other problems with tests and trace and  i think if you look at what kier starmer  has said today  and in terms of the five-point plan to  try and get the country  back on even keel i think that's very  clear in terms of what needs to be done  we've got lots of areas in local  lockdown we've got confused messaging  we've got a prime minister that doesn't  know  what the messaging is we've got areas  like bury and bolton and bunny and  lockdown when in actual fact they have  at lower infection rates in our rates  than perhaps say oxbridge where the  prime minister's constituency  is and i think somebody said yesterday  an academic said you could drive 40  miles across the northwest of england  and go through four different areas  with four different covered restrictions  so we really need the government to  start showing us what the criteria is  for putting  areas into local lockdown what the  criteria is for bringing us out of local  lockdown  fixing tests and trades and really if  everyone wants to download the  covered apps in both scotland and those  apps should be able to you should be  able to pop in your postcode because the  app tells you where you are  and give you a list of the local  restrictions it seems strange that  newspapers and broadcasting outlets can  do this on their websites but the  government can't do it on their own app  so let's learn from some of the  countries has already been said like  germany  who's publishing the criteria for local  people to see and let's try and get the  country  out of this as quickly as possible with  a sensible government with a  communication strategy that doesn't seem  completely haphazard  remember um just finally  a book called left out released last  month revealed that you almost left the  labour party last year there was  actually a pitch review  rehearsing uh your speech uh at a launch  event of the independent group of course  seven  uh labour mps quit the party to form the  group apparently you pulled out at the  last minute  none of them are in parliament you're in  the shadow cabinet did you dodge a bit  of a bullet there  well i think i made the correct decision  to stay and i think over that period of  time many  people in the labour party whether it be  the plp or ordinary members  it looked very seriously whether or not  the labour party still held the values  that they held and  that was  speech actually it was just we were  giving bits of paper to see what we  would uh  what it would look like and what we  would do and i pulled out um  quite before the change uk people did  leave and i did change my mind because  of a number of reasons the labour party  across the united kingdom still the only  party that speaks for the whole of the  united kingdom  and is the only party that can deliver  the social change and the social justice  that i came into the labour party to do  i want to fight  against that inequality and against  poverty and the labour party can do that  i'm glad i stayed  and we're now under new leadership and  new management because stammer is doing  incredibly well i think the public are  starting to respond to that  i'm disappointed some people in the end  did leave and history will show that  they did it for the right reasons  and many people including in the  conservative party of course  and in other parties liberal democrats  millers really examined whether or not  they would stay in their parties over  that tomorrow's period  i made a decision to stay and i'm very  glad that i did

